{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"carried_from":"prior-1","checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the nginx `location /mcp/` + `proxy_pass` with the server's `/mcp` default http_path (align trailing slash, or set http_path=\"/mcp/\", or use `proxy_pass .../mcp;`).","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["docs/mcp-auth.md:258: `location /mcp/ {`","docs/mcp-auth.md:259: `    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;`","docs/config-reference.md:98: | `mcp.http_path` | `str` | `'/mcp'` | Sets the request path served by the MCP HTTP transport. | active |","src/rebar/mcp_server.py:625: `streamable_http_path=path,` where `path = mcp_cfg.http_path` (mcp_server.py:525) — server mounts at `/mcp`, not `/mcp/`","The §7 config toml block (docs/mcp-auth.md:242-252) omits http_path, so default `/mcp` applies while the location and external URL are `/mcp/`."],"finding":"The §7 nginx recipe uses `location /mcp/` with a bare `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;` (no URI part), so nginx forwards the unmodified request URI `/mcp/` (trailing slash) to the loopback server, whose MCP endpoint default path is `/mcp` (no trailing slash, per mcp.http_path default). The trailing-slash mismatch can cause an operator who copies this recipe verbatim to get a 404/redirect instead of a working endpoint; the §7 config block also does not set http_path so the default `/mcp` applies.","id":"0","impact":0.6,"location":"docs/mcp-auth.md:258","norm_id":"n3d0e9650ba4aec18","priority":0.5143,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","assert